From 91d75d8064bbaa6d7a94a67d550a44025880011b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuya Fujiwara <hzw1258@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 11:15:23 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 12/17] Add date conversion with configurable formats
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Introduce DateRewriter to karukan-engine that transforms relative-day
readings (きょう, あした, etc.) into calendar dates with user-configurable
strftime formats. The rewriter uses an injectable Clock abstraction for
date sourcing, enabling deterministic testing while using the system
clock at runtime.

Integrate the feature into karukan-im's engine via EngineConfig and
expose configuration in the user's config.toml:
- date.enabled: toggles the feature on/off (default: true)
- date.formats: list of strftime formats for output (default: ISO and
  Japanese formats)

Add comprehensive tests for the rewriter and integration tests
exercising the full conversion path through the engine. Document the
feature in karukan-im's README with supported readings and configuration
details.
